\psdots[dotsize=5pt 0,dotstyle=*](4.,-2.)
\rput[bl](4.341588611333827,-2.3229444176719087){\darkgray{$B$}}

\end{pspicture*}
\end{center}

Determine the coefficients $a$ and $b$ of the quadratic equation\\ $x^2+a\cdot x + b = 0$ such that the two solutions to this equation are the $x$-coordinates of the points of intersection $A$ and $B$.

\antwort{$x^2-4\cdot x -2 = x-6$

