Verdoppelt man den Radius $r$ und die Höhe $h$ eines Zylinders, so erhält man einen Zylinder, dessen Volumen $x$-mal so groß wie jenes des ursprünglichen Zylinders ist.

Gib $x$ an!\vspace{0,3cm}

$x=$\,\antwort[\rule{3cm}{0.3pt}]{$8$}

463.content_translation:
The volume of a cylinder can be given by a function $V$ of the two quantities $h$ and $r$. The height of the cylinder is given by $h$ and the radius of the (circular) base is given by $r$.

Doubling the radius $r$ and the height $h$ of a cylinder, we obtain a cylinder whose volume will be $x$ times as big as the volume of the original cylinder.\\
Determine $x$.\vspace{0,3cm}

$x=$\,\antwort[\rule{3cm}{0.3pt}]{$8$}

