The function $f$ is known to have both of the properties given below:
\begin{itemize}
	\item The (smallest) period of the function $f$ is $\pi$.
	\item The difference between the largest and smallest value of the function $f$ is 6.
\end{itemize}

Write down $a$ and $b$.\vspace{0,3cm}

$a=$\,\antwort[\rule{3cm}{0.3pt}]{3}\vspace{0,3cm}

