949.content_translation:
Whilst entering a sporting event a person $P$ is carrying a prohibited item. During a security check, prohibited items are discovered with a probability of $0.9$. As this sporting event is particularly high-risk, each person must undergo such two independent security checks.

Determine the probability that person $P$’s prohibited item will be discovered by the security checks.

\antwort{$0,9+0,1\cdot 0,9=0,99$}

