The linear function $K$ describes the costs $K(x)$ in euros in terms of the number $x$ of items produced.\\
The linear function $E$ describes the revenue $E(x)$ in euros in terms of the number $x$ of items sold.

The diagram below shows the graph of the function $K$ and the graph of the function $E$.

\begin{center}
\psset{xunit=1.3cm,yunit=1.3cm,algebraic=true,dimen=middle,dotstyle=o,dotsize=5pt 0,linewidth=0.8pt,arrowsize=3pt 2,arrowinset=0.25}
