1295.content_translation:
A wheel of fortune with 24 equally sized sectors is spun. Two of the sectors are green; all the others are red.

For each spin:
\begin{itemize}
\item The pointer lands in each sector with equal probability.
\item If the pointer lands in a green sector, a prize is won.
\item If the pointer lands in a red sector, no prize is won.
\end{itemize}

The wheel of fortune is spun $n$ times. The results of the spins are independent of each other.

Write down the expected value for the number of prizes won in terms of $n$.

\antwort{$n\cdot\dfrac{1}{12}$}

1297.content:
