The following statements hold:
\begin{itemize}
\item If the value of the argument $x$ is doubled, then the corresponding value of the function reduces to a quarter of the original value of the function.
\item The point $(2, 2)$ lies on the graph of $f$.
\end{itemize}

Write down the values of $a$ and $z$.\vspace{0,5cm}

$z=\,\antwort[\rule{2cm}{0.3pt}]{-2}$\vspace{0,5cm}

$a=\,\antwort[\rule{2cm}{0.3pt}]{8}$

