\cellcolor[gray]{0.9}Linz&27\,\%&22\,\%\\ \hline
\end{tabular}\vspace{-0,3cm}

\tiny\flushleft\hspace{2cm} Table 1
\end{center}

The proportions of people who evaluated the product as ``very good'' are given in Table 2. For example: The value 15\,\% in Table 2 means that 15\,\% of all people aged 20 to under 40 in Vienna surveyed evaluated the product as ``very good''.

\begin{center}
\begin{tabular}{|l|c|c|}\cline{2-3}
\multicolumn{1}{l|}{\phantom{*}}&\cellcolor[gray]{0.9}20- to under 40-year-olds&\cellcolor[gray]{0.9}40- to 60-year-olds\\ \hline
