Workers in Austria have to pay part of their annual income $E$ to the state in the form of income tax $L$ ($E$, $L$ in \euro).\\
The table below shows how the corresponding income tax $L$ was determined for each annual income $E$ from \EUR{0} to \EUR{31\,000} for the year 2022.

\begin{center}
\begin{tabular}{|l|l|}\hline
\cellcolor[gray]{0.9}annual income $E$ in \euro &\cellcolor[gray]{0.9} income tax $L$ in \euro\\ \hline
$E\leq 11\,000$&$0$\\ \hline
$11\,000<E\leq 18\,000$&$20\,\%$ von $(E-11\,000)$\\ \hline
$18\,000<E\leq 31\,000$&$1\,400+[30\,\%$ von $(E-18\,000)]$\\ \hline
