The velocity of elevators for transporting people can vary greatly depending on construction and building height.

The following illustration shows the time-acceleration diagram for an elevator ride of 20 seconds. At the beginning and end of the ride the elevator is at a standstill. The time $t$ is measured in seconds, the acceleration $a(t)$ in m/s$^2$. The acceleration values were determined by sensors and the course of the acceleration is modelled by a derivable function $a$.

