The number of electric cars has increased in Austria in the last few years. The reasons for this include, among others, technical improvements, such as the increasing capacity of batteries and shorter charging times.

The \textit{Battery capacity} is understood to be the maximum energy $E$ (in kilowatt hours, kWh) that can be stored in the battery of the electric car. This energy is converted into a different form of energy while driving and is replenished when the car is charged.

The \textit{charging time} is understood to be the time that is required to fully charge a (nearly) empty battery.%Aufgabentext

\begin{aufgabenstellung}
