\end{center}%Aufgabentext

The difference equation $B_{n+1}=B_n\cdot a+b$ gives the development of the number of electric cars in Austria starting from the year 2015 for the years 2016 and 2017.\\
For this equation, the following conditions hold:\vspace{-0,2cm}
\begin{itemize}
\item $B_0$ is the number at the end of the year 2015.\\
\item $B_1$ is the number at the end of the year 2016.\\
\item $B_2$ is the number at the end of the year 2017.
\end{itemize}

\Subitem{Write down the values of $a$ and $b$.\vspace{0,3cm}

$a=$\,\antwort[\rule{3cm}{0.3pt}]{$1,37\ldots$}\vspace{0,3cm}

$b=$\,\antwort[\rule{3cm}{0.3pt}]{$2\,168,1\ldots$}} %Unterpunkt1

So that the difference equation given above also holds for the year 2018, the number of electric cars would have had to have risen in the rest of 2018 by a particular number.

\Subitem{Determine this number.} %Unterpunkt2

\item The battery capacity (in kWh) is the product of the charging capacity (in kW) and the charging time (in h). For example, in order to charge a (nearly) empty battery with a battery capacity of 22\,kWh with a charging capacity of 11\,kW, a charging time of 2\,h is necessary.

The function $f$ describes the charging time $f(P)$ of a battery with a battery capacity of 22\,kWh in terms of the charging capacity $P$ ($P$ in kW, $f(P)$ in h).%Aufgabentext

\Subitem{Write down $f(P)$.\vspace{0,3cm}

$f(P)=$\,\antwort[\rule{3cm}{0.3pt}]{$\frac{22}{P}$}} %Unterpunkt1

The typical charging capacity of a private charging station lies in the capacity interval [2.3\,kW, 3.7\,kW].

\Subitem{For a battery with a battery capacity of 22\,kWh, write down the time interval for the charging time that corresponds to this capacity interval.} %Unterpunkt2

\item The following assumptions are made in order to model an electric car driving on a particular test track:\vspace{-0,2cm}

