%Aufgabentext

\begin{aufgabenstellung}
\item In a particular game, the ball has a velocity vector of $\vec{v}=\binom{4}{7}$ pixels per image when it hits the upper edge of the playing field.%Aufgabentext

\Subitem{Determine the angle $\alpha$ at which the ball hits the edge of the playing field.\vspace{0,3cm}

	$\alpha$= \antwort[\rule{5cm}{0.3pt}]{$60.26^\circ$}} %Unterpunkt1

	The velocity vector always has integer components. Assume that the sum of the absolute values of the components can never be greater than 20.

\Subitem{The ball is reflected by the upper edge of the playing field at an angle of $\beta$. What is the smallest value, $\beta_\text{min}$, that the angle $\beta$ can have under these conditions? Determine $\beta_\text{min}$.\vspace{0,3cm}

	$\beta_\text{min}$= \antwort[\rule{5cm}{0.3pt}]{$3,01^\circ$}} %Unterpunkt2

\item In another game, the ball is at point $(401, 301)$ and its velocity vector is $\vec{v}=\binom{2}{-3}$ pixels per image.%Aufgabentext

\Subitem{Determine how many \textit{seconds} it takes for the ball to be reflected by the lower edge of the playing field.} %Unterpunkt1

After this reflection the ball moves in a straight line until it hits either a paddle or the edge of the playing field.

\Subitem{Determine the vector equation of this straight line.} %Unterpunkt2

\item Two children, Nicola and Florian, have been playing \textit{Pong} against each other for a long time. Out of 45 games, Nicola has won 31 times and Florian has won 14 times.%Aufgabentext

\Subitem{On the basis of this information, find a symmetrical 95\,\% confidence interval for the probability that Nicola wins.} %Unterpunkt1
