When a radioactive substance decays, the number of nuclei still to decay decreases exponentially and can be approximated by the function $N$ where $N(t)=N_0\cdot e^{-\lambda\cdot t}$. In this function, $N_0$ is the number of atomic nuclei at time $t=0$, $N(t)$ gives the number of nuclei still to decay at time $t\geq 0$, and $\lambda$ is the so-called decay constant.

The activity, $A(t)$, is given by the absolute value of the instantaneous rate of change of the function $N$ at time $t$. It is measured in Becquerels (Bq). An activity of 1\,Bq corresponds to one decay per second.

For radioactive substances, the activity also decreases exponentially and can be modelled by a function $A$, where $A(t)=A_0\cdot e^{-\lambda\cdot t}$. In this function, $A_0$ gives the activity at time $t=0$ and $A(t)$ gives the activity at time $t\geq 0$.%Aufgabentext

\begin{aufgabenstellung}
\item %Aufgabentext

\Subitem{Write down a formula using which the original number of atomic nuclei, $N_0$, can be calculated from the observed activity, $A_0$.} %Unterpunkt1

A sample of $^{238}$U (uranium 238) has an activity of 17\,Bq at time $t=0$. The decay constant of $^{238}$U is $\lambda\approx 4.92\cdot 10^{-18}$ per second.

\Subitem{Determine the number of $^{238}$U nuclei in the sample at time $t=0$.} %Unterpunkt2

\item Using the amount of the carbon isotope $^{14}$C contained in a sample, the age of the sample can be determined. Due to the metabolic process, an equilibrium concentration of $^{14}$C and/or an activity of about 0.267\,Bq per gram of carbon had adjusted between the formation and the decay of the isotope, in the atmosphere as well as in living organisms. With the dying of an organism (e. g. a tree), the absorption of $^{14}$C ends. The $^{14}$C-amount decreases from this point of time exponentially (with a decay constant of $\lambda\approx 1,21\cdot 10^{-4}$ per year) and with it, the activity also begins to decrease exponentially.%Aufgabentext

\Subitem{A wooden artefact contains 25 grams of carbon and has an activity of around 4\,Bq.\\
Determine how many years ago this wood has died.} %Unterpunkt1
\Subitem{Determine whether more or fewer than half of the original number of $^{14}$C atoms had decayed by the time the artefact was found and justify your answer.} %Unterpunkt2

\item The function $N$ can also be written in the form $N(t)=N_0\cdot 0.5^{\frac{t}{c}}$ where $c\in\mathbb{R}^+$.%Aufgabentext

\Subitem{Determine the relationship between the constant $c$ and the half-life of a radioactive substance, $\tau$.} %Unterpunkt1
\Subitem{In the diagram below, the graph of a function $N$ is shown, where\\ $N(t)=N_0\cdot 0.5^{\frac{t}{c}}$ with $c\in\mathbb{R}^+$.

	On this diagram, draw the graph of a function $N_{\text{new}}$, where\\ $N_{\text{new}}(t)=N_0\cdot 0.5^{\frac{t}{c_{\text{new}}}}$ with $c_{\text{new}}\in\mathbb{R}^+$ given that $c_{\text{new}}<c$.\vspace{0,3cm}

		\begin{center}
