In order to monitor the development of a child’s height and mass, the percentile curves for height (in cm) and mass (in kg) are provided in the baby’s ‘Developmental Record Book’. Percentiles split the heights and masses of children into percentage-areas. If a value lies on the 10$^\text{th}$ percentile curve for height, this means that 10\,\% of children at this age are shorter than or the same height as this value, and 90\,\% are taller than or the same height as this value.\\
It is common to describe all values between the 3$^\text{rd}$ and 97$^\text{th}$ percentiles as ``normal''. The following diagram shows the height and body mass curves for boys aged between 0 and 18 years:

