$x$ corresponds to the horizontal distance of the car (which is here modelled as a point) from the point $A$ and $h(x)$ gives the height of the position of the car above the height of point $A$ ($h(x)$ in m, $x$ in m). In this model, the points $A$ and $B$ have coordinates $A=(0,0)$ and $B=(60,10)$.

