\item The area of the Pasterze, which was around 30\,km$^2$ in 1856, had reduced to about half of this value by 2006. The volume of ice of the Pasterze was around 1.7\,km$^3$ in 2006. One possible method for calculating an approximation of the volume of ice of the Pasterze in 1856 is to assume that the ice reduced in all three dimensions by the same factor. This simplification means that the glacier in 2006 is a scaled down version of the glacier from 1856.%Aufgabentext

\Subitem{Write down the approximate value for the volume of ice (in km$^3$) of the Pasterze in 1856 obtained using this method.} %Unterpunkt1

