The table below shows estimates of the global population (in the middle of each year) for certain years.

\begin{center}
\begin{tabular}{|c|c|}\hline
\cellcolor[gray]{0.9}year&\cellcolor[gray]{0.9}global population in billions\\ \hline
1850&1.260\\ \hline
1900&1.650\\ \hline
1950&2.536\\ \hline
1960&3.030\\ \hline
1970&3.700\\ \hline
1990&5.327\\ \hline
2000&6.140\\ \hline
2010&6.957\\ \hline
2020&7.790\\ \hline
\end{tabular}
\end{center}
%Aufgabentext

\begin{aufgabenstellung}
\item In the time period from 1850 to 1950, the global population roughly doubled. Assume that for this time period, the global population increased by the same percentage each year.%Aufgabentext

\Subitem{Determine this percentage.} %Unterpunkt1

\item From 1970, the development of the global population can be approximated by a linear function $f$.%Aufgabentext

\Subitem{Using the values for the global population in the years 1970 and 2000, write down an equation of the function $f$ in terms of the time $t$ ($t$ in years with $t=0$ for the year 1970, $f(t)$ in billions).} %Unterpunkt1
\Subitem{Determine the percentage by which the value for 2020 calculated using the function $f$ differs from the value for 2020 given in the table above.} %Unterpunkt2

\item In another model, the development of the global population from 1970 is modelled by the function $g$.

$g(t)=3{.}7\cdot e^{-0{.}0001\cdot t^2+0{.}02\cdot t}$

$t\ldots$ time from 1970 in years\\
$g(t)\ldots$ global population at time $t$ in billions

According to this model, the global population will first increase before it begins to decrease.%Aufgabentext

\Subitem{Using the function $g$, determine the maximum value of the global population and the calendar year in which this value should occur according to the model.\vspace{0,3cm}

maximum global population: around \antwort[\rule{3cm}{0.3pt}]{10,1} billion\vspace{0,3cm}

calendar year: \antwort[\rule{3cm}{0.3pt}]{2070}} %Unterpunkt1

\end{aufgabenstellung}

\begin{loesung}
\item \subsection{Lösungserwartung:} 

\Subitem{$\sqrt[100]{\frac{2,536}{1,250}}=1,00701\ldots$

oder:

$\sqrt[100]{2}=1,00695\ldots$

Prozentsatz: rund 0,70\,\%} %Lösung von Unterpunkt1

