There are various pools in a swimming centre.%Aufgabentext

\begin{aufgabenstellung}
\item The volume of a particular cuboid-shaped swimming pool can be described by the equation $V=a^2\cdot h$.

$a\ldots$ side length of the square base\\
$h\ldots$ depth of the swimming pool

The function $V$: $\mathbb{R}^+\rightarrow\mathbb{R}^+$, $a\mapsto V(a)$ with constant $h$ and the function $h$: $\mathbb{R}^+\rightarrow\mathbb{R}^+$, $V\mapsto h(V)$ with constant $a$ are to be considered.%Aufgabentext

\Subitem{\englueckentext{
				text={The function $V$ is a \gap; the function $h$ is a \gap}, 	%Lueckentext Luecke=\gap
