$T=$\,\antwort[\rule{3cm}{0.3pt}]{$\dfrac{38}{p}$}} %Unterpunkt1

The amount of water in this swimming pool decreases due to evaporation and operational causes. The function $W$: $[0;10]\rightarrow\mathbb{R}$ with $W(t)=-\frac{1}{96}\cdot t^3+\frac{1}{4}\cdot t^2-\frac{35}{24}\cdot t$ models the instantaneous rate of change of the amount of water at time $t$ on a particular day ($t$ in h, $W(t)$ in m$^3$/h).

