\psdots[dotstyle=*](7.07,0.35)
\end{scriptsize}
\end{pspicture*}
\end{center}%Aufgabentext

The path of the mountain hike has a gradient of $a\,\%$.

\Subitem{Determine $a$.\vspace{0,5cm}

$a=$\,\antwort[\rule{3cm}{0.3pt}]{$39,5\ldots$}\,\%} %Unterpunkt1

\item The fitness watch \textit{Sporty} is particularly popular.\\
The probability that a randomly chosen person in Austria possesses a \textit{Sporty} fitness watch is $p$.

In the course of a study, 160 randomly chosen people in Austria are surveyed.

The binomially distributed random variable $X$ gives the number of people out of the 160 people surveyed who possess a \textit{Sporty} fitness watch.%Aufgabentext

\Subitem{\englueckentext[-0.29]{
				text={The probability that none of the 160 people surveyed possesses a \textit{Sporty} fitness watch is \gap; the probability that at least 2 of the 160 people surveyed possess a \textit{Sporty} fitness watch is \gap.}, 	%Lueckentext Luecke=\gap
				L1={$1-p$}, 		%1.Moeglichkeit links  
				L2={$p^{160}$}, 		%2.Moeglichkeit links
				L3={$(1-p)^{160}$}, 		%3.Moeglichkeit links
				R1={$1-\left[\binom{160}{0}\cdot p^0\cdot(1-p)^{160}+\binom{160}{1}\cdot p\cdot(1-p)^{159}\right]$}, 		%1.Moeglichkeit rechts 
				R2={$\binom{160}{0}\cdot p^0\cdot(1-p)^{160}+\binom{160}{1}\cdot p\cdot(1-p)^{159}$}, 		%2.Moeglichkeit rechts
				R3={$\binom{160}{2}\cdot p^2\cdot(1-p)^{158}$}, 		%3.Moeglichkeit rechts
				%% LOESUNG: %%
				A1=3,   % Antwort links
				A2=1		% Antwort rechts 
				}} %Unterpunkt1

\item Fitness watches show, among other things, the calories burned during a sports activity. In the course of a study, the percentage deviation of the actual calories burned for a sports activity from the corresponding value measured by the fitness watch was investigated for 60 people. These deviations along with their corresponding absolute frequencies are summarized in classes in the table below.

\begin{center}
\begin{tabular}{|c|c|}\hline
