If only the other drain is opened, then the complete drainage of the pond takes 6\,h.\\
Each of the drainage velocities is constant over the whole time period.\\
The time it takes for the pond to be completely drained when both drains are opened at the
same time is given by $T$.%Aufgabentext

\Subitem{Determine $T$.} %Unterpunkt1

\item The completely empty pond is filled again with 129\,m$^3$ of water

The function $d$: $\mathbb{R}^+\rightarrow\mathbb{R}^+$ gives the filling time $d(z)$ in terms of the constant inflow velocity $z$ ($z$ in m$^3$/h, $d(z)$ in h).%Aufgabentext

