The function $h$ describes the height of the surface of the water above the deepest point of the pond in terms of the time $t$ for a constant inflow velocity $z=6$\,m$^3$/h ($t$ in h, $h(t)$ in m).

The following holds for the instantaneous rate of change of the height of the surface of the
water:\vspace{0,2cm}

$h'(t)=\dfrac{15}{\sqrt{2\,738\cdot\pi\cdot t}}$ with $t>0$

