Two straight rays of light leave the light source $L$ and are deflected at points $P$ and $Q$ on the reflector parallel to the $x$-axis towards a wall. They hit the wall at points $A$ and $B$.

$L=(2{.}5, 0)$\\
$\overline{LP}=3$\,cm and $\overline{LQ}=4{.}1$\,cm\\
$A=(20, y_A)$ and $B=(20, y_B)$\\
$m=19{.}5$\,cm\vspace{0,3cm}

$\overline{LP}+m=\overline{LQ}+n$
%Aufgabentext

\Subitem{Determine $y_B$.} %Unterpunkt1

\item  During a quality control procedure, torches are checked for faults $F_1$, $F_2$ and $F_3$. These 3 faults
occur independently.

The table below shows these faults along with their corresponding probabilities.

\begin{center}
\begin{tabular}{|c|l|c|}\hline
\cellcolor[gray]{0.9}fault&\cellcolor[gray]{0.9}description&\cellcolor[gray]{0.9}probability\\ \hline
$F_1$&The torch is defective.&$p_1$\\ \hline
$F_2$&The torch is the wrong colour.&$0{.}02$\\ \hline
$F_3$&The torch has no storage bag.&$0{.}01$\\ \hline
\end{tabular}
\end{center}

A torch is selected at random and checked.
%Aufgabentext

\Subitem{Match each of the four events to the probability they definitely correspond to from A to F.

\zuordnen{
				R1={The torch is defective and is the
wrong colour.},				% Response 1
				R2={The torch is the correct colour.},				% Response 2
				R3={The torch is not defective, it is the
correct colour, and it does not have a storage bag.},				% Response 3
				R4={The torch exhibits at least 1 of
these 3 faults.},				% Response 4
				%% Moegliche Zuordnungen: %%
				A={$0{.}98$}, 				%Moeglichkeit A  
				B={$1-(1-p_1)\cdot 0{.}98\cdot 0{.}99$}, 				%Moeglichkeit B  
				C={$p_1\cdot 0{.}02$}, 				%Moeglichkeit C  
				D={$1-p_1\cdot 0{.}02\cdot 0{.}01$}, 				%Moeglichkeit D  
				E={$p_1\cdot 0{.}02\cdot 0{.}01$}, 				%Moeglichkeit E  
				F={$(1-p_1)\cdot 0{.}98\cdot 0{.}01$}, 				%Moeglichkeit F  
				%% LOESUNG: %%
				A1={C},				% 1. richtige Zuordnung
				A2={A},				% 2. richtige Zuordnung
				A3={F},				% 3. richtige Zuordnung
				A4={B},				% 4. richtige Zuordnung
				}
} %Unterpunkt1

\item The total costs for the production of the torches in terms of the amount produced $x$ can be modelled by the differentiable cost function $K$.

$x\ldots$ amount produced in units of quantity (ME)\\
$E(x)\ldots$ total costs for the production of $x$ units in monetary units (GE)\\

The corresponding marginal cost function $K'$ has the equation\\
$K'(x)=0{.}33\cdot x^2-1{.}8\cdot x+3$

$K(1)=44{.}21$ holds.

\Subitem{Write down an equation of the function $K$.\vspace{0,5cm}

$K(x)=\,\antwort[\rule{5cm}{0.3pt}]{0,11\cdot x^3-0,9\cdot x^2+3\cdot x+42}$}

It can be assumed that every torch produced is also sold.

The revenue from the sale of these torches can be modelled by the function $E$ in terms of the amount produced $x$.

$E(x)=a\cdot x$

$x\ldots$ amount produced in ME\\
$E(x)\ldots$ revenue for the amount produced $x$ in GE\\
$a\ldots$ price in GE/ME

The profit is modelled by the profit function $G$ ($x$ in ME, $G(x)$ in GE).

The business goal is to generate a profit of at least 100\,GE for the production and sale of 5\,ME of torches.

\Subitem{Determine the lowest possible price with which this business goal can be achieved.}
%Aufgabentext

\end{aufgabenstellung}

\begin{loesung}
\item \subsection{Lösungserwartung:} 

\Subitem{$3+19,5=4,1+n$

$n=18,4$

$y_B=\sqrt{4,1^2-(18,4-17,5)^2}=4$} %Lösung von Unterpunkt1

\setcounter{subitemcounter}{0}
\subsection{Lösungsschlüssel:}

\Subitem{Ein Punkt für das richtige Berechnen von $y_B$.} %Lösungschlüssel von Unterpunkt1

\item \subsection{Lösungserwartung:} 

\Subitem{siehe oben} %Lösung von Unterpunkt1

\setcounter{subitemcounter}{0}
\subsection{Lösungsschlüssel:}

\Subitem{Ein Punkt für vier richtige Zuordnungen, ein halber Punkt für zwei oder drei richtige Zuordnungen.} %Lösungschlüssel von Unterpunkt1

\item \subsection{Lösungserwartung:} 

\Subitem{$K(x)=0,11\cdot x^3-0,9\cdot x^2+3\cdot x+42$} %Lösung von Unterpunkt1
\Subitem{$G(x)=a\cdot x-(0,11\cdot x^3-0,9\cdot x^2+3\cdot x+42)$

$G(5)\geq 100$\vspace{0,3cm}

Berechnung mittels Technologieeinsatz:

$a\geq 29,65$\vspace{0,3cm}

Der kleinstmögliche Preis beträgt 29,65\,GE/ME} %%Lösung von Unterpunkt2

\setcounter{subitemcounter}{0}
\subsection{Lösungsschlüssel:}

\Subitem{Ein Punkt für das richtige Aufstellen der Funktionsgleichung von $K$.} %Lösungschlüssel von Unterpunkt1
\Subitem{Ein Punkt für das richtige Berechnen.} %Lösungschlüssel von Unterpunkt2

\end{loesung}

