\item For speeds from 10\,kn to 30\,kn, the fuel consumption of a particular container ship can be modelled in terms of the speed by the function $f$.%Aufgabentext

$f(v)=a\cdot v^3+b$

$v \ldots$ speed in kn\\
$f(v) \ldots$ fuel consumption at speed $v$ in kg/NM\\
$a,b \ldots$ real parameters

The following statements hold:
\begin{itemize}
\item At a speed of 10\,kn, the fuel consumption is 90\,kg/NM.
\item At a speed of 25\,kn, the fuel consumption is 260\,kg/NM.
\end{itemize}

\Subitem{Determine the coefficients $a$ and $b$.} %Unterpunkt1

\item For every journey of a particular container ship, both filled as well as empty containers are transported.

The corresponding number of filled and empty containers for 10 particular journeys is shown in the table below.%Aufgabentext

\begin{center}
