\Subitem{Determine the probability that at most 1 reservation is cancelled on New Year’s Eve.} %Unterpunkt1

\item In a particular year, there were on average 4 100 overnight stays per month in this hotel.

In the first 6 months of this year (January to June), there were on average 4\,000 overnight stays per month.

The table below gives the number of overnight stays for the other months of this year ($n,d\in\mathbb{N}$).%Aufgabentext

\begin{center}
