\end{pspicture*}
\end{center}

%Aufgabentext

\Subitem{Determine the length of the runway.} %Unterpunkt1

The \textit{Mount Everest Trek} runs from Lukla airport to the base camp and is completed on foot.\\
The prevailing low air pressure there makes this trek particularly demanding.

Lukla airport lies 2 860\,m above sea level.\\
The base camp lies 5 364\,m above sea level.

It can be assumed that the air pressure reduces exponentially with increasing height above sea level.

For an increase in height above sea level of 80 m, the air pressure reduces by 1\,\%.

On a particular day, the air pressure at Lukla airport is 708 hectopascals (hPa).

\Subitem{Under this assumption, determine the air pressure at the base camp on this day.} %Unterpunkt2

\item The course of the marathon goes from the starting point at the base camp to the end point in Namche. At particular waypoints, the time taken for a particular runner to reach these waypoints is recorded (see table below).\vspace{0,1cm}

\begin{tabular}{|p{3cm}|p{4cm}|p{4cm}|}
\cellcolor[gray]{0.9}name of the waypoint&\cellcolor[gray]{0.9}the distance covered until this waypoint in km&\cellcolor[gray]{0.9}the time taken to reach this waypoint in h\\ \hline
base camp&$0$&$0$\\ \hline
Dingboche&$17,3$&$t_1$\\ \hline
Tengboche&$32,6$&$t_2$\\ \hline
Namche&$42,195$&$t_3$\\ \hline
\end{tabular}

The expected time $t_3$ to complete the whole marathon can be approximated using the time $t_1$ and the following formula:

$t_3=t_1\cdot\left(\dfrac{42,195}{17,3}\right)^k$\vspace{0,2cm}

$t_3\ldots$ the expected time for the whole marathon in $h$\\
$t_1\ldots$ the time taken to reach the waypoint Dingboche in $h$\\
$k>0\ldots$ fatigue factor

For this runner, $k=1,073$ holds.

The runner sets off from the base camp at 07:00 (07:00:00). At 08:30 (08:30:00), she reaches the waypoint Dingboche. According to the model above, the runner reaches the finish line in Namche at a particular time of day.
%Aufgabentext

\Subitem{For this particular time of day, write down the hours and minutes in the boxes provided below.\vspace{0,5cm}

time of day: \antwort[\rule{1cm}{0.3pt}]{10} : \antwort[\rule{1cm}{0.3pt}]{54} : 16} %Unterpunkt1

\item After completing the marathon, two values are calculated for all runners as part of the race analysis:
\begin{itemize}
\item the average speed $\overline{v}$ (in km/h)
\item the pace $c$ (in min/km)
\end{itemize}

The pace gives the average number of minutes required per kilometer.

%Aufgabentext

\Subitem{\englueckentext{
				text={The pace $c$ can be calculated using the equation \gap, and it \gap if the average speed $\overline{v}$ doubles.}, 	%Lueckentext Luecke=\gap
				L1={$c=\dfrac{60}{\overline{v}}$}, 		%1.Moeglichkeit links  
				L2={$c=\dfrac{1}{\overline{v}}$}, 		%2.Moeglichkeit links
				L3={$c=\dfrac{3,6}{\overline{v}}$}, 		%3.Moeglichkeit links
				R1={halves}, 		%1.Moeglichkeit rechts 
				R2={doubles}, 		%2.Moeglichkeit rechts
				R3={quadruples}, 		%3.Moeglichkeit rechts
				%% LOESUNG: %%
				A1=1,   % Antwort links
				A2=1		% Antwort rechts 
				}} %Unterpunkt1

\end{aufgabenstellung}

\begin{loesung}
\item \subsection{Lösungserwartung:} 

\Subitem{$\alpha\ldots$ Steigungswinkel der Landebahn in $^\circ$\\
$x\ldots$ Länge der Landebahn in m

$\tan(\alpha)=0,117$\\
$\alpha=6,673\ldots^\circ$

$\sin(6,673\ldots^\circ)=\frac{61}{x}$\\
$x=524,9\ldots$

\textit{oder:}

$h\ldots$ horizontale Entfernung zwischen Anfang und Ende der Landebahn in m

$\frac{61}{h}=0,117$

$h=521,367\ldots$

$x=\sqrt{h^2+61^2}=524,9\ldots$

Die Landebahn hat eine Länge von rund 525\,m} %Lösung von Unterpunkt1
\Subitem{$\dfrac{5\,364-2\,860}{80}=31,3$

$708\cdot 0,99^{31,3}=516,9\ldots$

Der Luftdruck im Basislager an diesem Tag beträgt rund 517\,hPa.} %%Lösung von Unterpunkt2

\setcounter{subitemcounter}{0}
\subsection{Lösungsschlüssel:}

\Subitem{Ein Punkt für das richtige Berechnen der Länge der Landebahn.} %Lösungschlüssel von Unterpunkt1
\Subitem{Ein Punkt für das richtige Berechnen des Luftdrucks im Basislager.} %Lösungschlüssel von Unterpunkt2

\item \subsection{Lösungserwartung:} 

\Subitem{$t_3=1,5\cdot\left(\dfrac{42,195}{17,3}\right)^{1,073}=3,904\ldots$\vspace{0,3cm}

$0,904\ldots\cdot 60=54,27\ldots$

Uhrzeit: 10:54:16} %Lösung von Unterpunkt1

\setcounter{subitemcounter}{0}
\subsection{Lösungsschlüssel:}

